  "question": {
    "text": "The time period of an earth satellite in circular orbit is independent of",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "R7f7p",
      "text": "\nthe mass of the satellite\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "jwRup",
      "text": "\nradius of its orbit\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "3mDkr",
      "text": "\nboth the mass and radius of the orbit\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "XJrlf",
      "text": "\nneither the mass of the satellite nor the radius of its orbit.",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "The time period of satellite is given by\n$$\nT=2 \\pi \\sqrt{\\frac{(\\mathrm{R}+\\mathrm{h})^3}{\\mathrm{GM}}}\n$$\nwhere, $\\mathrm{R}+\\mathrm{h}=$ radius of orbit satellite, $\\mathrm{M}=$ mass of earth.",
    "image": null
  },
